==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat Mask Doron''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Awakened Doron''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit|Behemoth Stones]] and XP after completing [[Atonement for Sin]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Like [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]], Elder Mask Doron is a suicide attacker that delivers a crowd-controlling status effect (in his case a 6.67-second freeze), giving other (especially fragile) units an expanded window of opportunity. Thanks to this, rushers like [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] can inflict much greater damage against relics that they normally wouldn't be able to due to the trait's generally high damage. Unlike Glass Cat, however, Doron can also deliver decent damage himself, as well as being able to hit multiple targets with his Omni strike and Surge. Keep in mind that the Surge is likely to hit backline enemies, due to its spawning range of 400~1,000.

He has generalist usage as a chipper as well. He is able to deliver guaranteed damage due to his high health and, as a bonus, can act as a shield for a brief moment. Combined with his low cost, this makes him helpful in chipping down bosses and clearing peons. However, do note that he is heavily reliant on his status effect against Relics, meaning that he will be significantly less effective against non-Relic enemies, and that his long recharge time will limit his usage.

==='''True Form'''===
Awakened Doron gains speed, Knockback, Colossus Slayer, and Behemoth Slayer. The increased speed is not necessarily a significant buff, but reaching the frontlines faster is still notable. The Knockback ability, however, is the biggest buff by far. It allows Awakened Doron to not only stop Relics from advancing, but also to push them back. Depending on the surge spawn, it can push midrangers such as [[M. Ost]] and [[Relic Bun-Bun]], or it can push backliners such as [[Lowkey]] and [[Golem Sunfish]]. However, while this ability does push enemies back and keep them at bay, it can also reduce the chip damage dealt by these surges. Depending on the stage, this tradeoff is usually worth it. However, if you are not lucky with the surges (which has a wide spawn range), his knockback can be detrimental if he doesn't hit the backliners.

Additionally, Behemoth Slayer and Colossus Slayer notably help. The increased HP and dodge chance are insignificant due to Awakened Doron's naturally high HP and the fact he destroys himself upon attacking once, but the increased damage from a level 3 surge can help dealing additional chip damage, though this is less usefulagainst Behemoths as many are Surge Immune. This works especially well against Relic Behemoth/Colossal enemies, such as [[Great Ape Luza]] and [[Zero Luza]] in the crowned difficulties. While Zero Luza is Freeze Immune, Knockback remains effective against it. While the extra damage is good against [[Ancient Magamojoe]], [[Ultima Beast Naala]] and [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]], their immunities can drastically reduce Doron's effectiveness. Outside of Relics, Behemoths, and Colossals, this True Form changes nothing significant for most enemies, so his generalist role as an occasional chipper is the exact same as before.

